# Mograph CLI

Create videos using AI paired with Claude Code / Codex.

The pipeline takes a **timeline JSON** (tracks of clips) and renders it: image generation → video generation → audio assembly. Mock mode runs the whole thing without API calls.

## Quick start

```bash
# Run full pipeline from a timeline file
python pipeline.py --timeline-file my-timeline.json --stage final

# Dry run (show execution plan without running)
python pipeline.py --timeline-file my-timeline.json --dry-run

# Mock mode (no API calls — uses fixtures)
python pipeline.py --mock --timeline-file my-timeline.json --stage final
```

For project-stable run dirs and auto-resume, use the `scripts/run.py` wrapper. To scaffold a new project (timeline + ref manifest + agent notes), use `scripts/init_project.py "Project Name"`.

---

## The three things you'll do most

### 1. Minimal video

One clip, no narration:

```json
{
  "version": 1,
  "project": { "name": "Single Clip" },
  "tracks": [{
    "id": "visuals", "type": "video",
    "clips": [{
      "id": "vid-1",
      "source": {
        "type": "video",
        "prompt": "A cat on a windowsill watching rain, soft lighting",
        "model": "seedance-2.0-fast",
        "duration": 6
      }
    }]
  }]
}
```

### 2. Use a reference image

Anchor a clip to a specific look — character sheet, environment, mood-board frame.

```json
{
  "id": "vid-1",
  "source": {
    "type": "video",
    "prompt": "Hero approaches the castle gate",
    "reference_images": ["refs/hero.png", "refs/castle.png"]
  }
}
```

Photoreal-human refs trip Seedance moderation (E005). Stylized refs (anime, claymation, illustration) work fine. To generate refs first, see [`docs/workflows/character-asset/`](docs/workflows/character-asset/).

### 3. Lock the style across clips

Pin a consistent look across every clip with a shared mood-board + a `prompt_prefix`:

```json
{
  "defaults": {
    "video": { "prompt_prefix": "In the same reference image style," }
  },
  "tracks": [{
    "id": "visuals", "type": "video",
    "clips": [
      { "id": "vid-1", "source": { "type": "video", "prompt": "fox in pine forest at dawn", "reference_images": ["assets/mood/01.jpg", "assets/mood/02.jpg"] } },
      { "id": "vid-2", "source": { "type": "video", "prompt": "fox crosses a frozen stream",  "reference_images": ["assets/mood/01.jpg", "assets/mood/02.jpg"] } }
    ]
  }]
}
```

Prefix is prepended to every clip's prompt; same refs on every clip lets the model average over them. To rip a style or format pack from an existing video, see [`docs/workflows/style-rip/`](docs/workflows/style-rip/) and [`docs/workflows/format-rip/`](docs/workflows/format-rip/).

